<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1910] .Net: Possible handle leak in ScanQuery</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1910</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;See ScanQuery.cs, &quot;writer.WriteObject(holder);&quot; line. If it fails due to user filter being non-serializable, we leak a handle.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Same thing in Cache.LoadCache&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Another leak is in Java. If the GridCloseableIteratorAdapter fails in ctor, it does not close keyValFilter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
